prompt:
Union-find over fixed-size element sets:

```c
void uf_init(int *parent, int *rank_, int n);
int uf_find(int *parent, int x);
void uf_union(int *parent, int *rank_, int a, int b);
int uf_connected(int *parent, int a, int b);
```

find uses path compression; union by rank; connected returns 1 iff same root.

tests.code:
int parent[8], rk[8];
uf_init(parent, rk, 8);
uf_union(parent, rk, 0, 1);
uf_union(parent, rk, 2, 3);
CHECK_EQ(uf_connected(parent, 0, 1), 1);
CHECK_EQ(uf_connected(parent, 0, 2), 0);
uf_union(parent, rk, 1, 2);
CHECK_EQ(uf_connected(parent, 0, 3), 1);

int parent2[4], rk2[4];
uf_init(parent2, rk2, 4);
uf_union(parent2, rk2, 0, 1);
int r1 = uf_find(parent2, 0);
int r2 = uf_find(parent2, 0);
CHECK_EQ(r1, r2);
CHECK_EQ(uf_find(parent2, 1), r1);
